{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtRRsGCHgH5Bez9dsERf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UmYyT1VKePGCrovgp75gt2","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-lAzs4w/ANSWER.md","content":"# Answer: save_fact was evicting the cached system prompt\n\n## Cause\n\n`build_system()` in `bot.py` put the static coaching rules (`INSTRUCTIONS`) and the\nper-athlete context (today's date, zones, goal, and the `facts` list) into one text\nblock and put `cache_control` on that block. The cache key is the whole block, so\nany change to the athlete's facts changed the block and invalidated the cache for\nthe static instructions too.\n\n`save_fact` appends to `facts`, so the next request after a save wrote the whole\nblock again (`cache_creation_input_tokens` ~1000, `cache_read_input_tokens: 0`).\nThis matches the pattern in `logs/usage.jsonl` and `NOTES.md`.\n\n## Change\n\n`bot.py`, `build_system()`. The system prompt is now two blocks:\n\n1. `INSTRUCTIONS`, with `cache_control: ephemeral`. It is identical for every athlete\n   and every day, so it stays cached across `save_fact` writes, across athletes, and\n   across the date change.\n2. `athlete_context(a, today)`, with no cache marker. It holds the date, zones, goal,\n   facts and language. It is small, and it is the only part that changes when a fact\n   is saved.\n\nThe cache prefix is `tools` + block 1. The `tools` list does not change on a `save_fact`\nbecause `save_fact` is a core tool, so a memory write now only re-sends the small\nathlete block.\n\nNo other behaviour changed. Message text, tools, and the tool loop are untouched.\n\n## Verification\n\nOffline, with a stub LLM and `save_athlete` patched out so `data/athletes.json` was\nnot written:\n\n- A message that triggers `save_fact` produced two requests. The static block was\n  byte-identical in both and carried `cache_control`. The athlete block had no marker\n  and did change (the new fact appeared).\n\nI did not call the Anthropic API, so the cache hit rate is not measured here. Check\nit on the next deploy: after a `save_fact`, the following round should show\n`cache_read_input_tokens` ≈ the static block size and `cache_creation_input_tokens`\nonly ≈ the athlete block.\n\n## Things to check or not yet fixed\n\n- **Minimum cacheable length.** Caching only applies above the model's minimum prefix\n  length (about 1024 tokens for Sonnet-class models). `INSTRUCTIONS` is about 2,500\n  characters, which is probably under 1,024 tokens on its own. The breakpoint still\n  covers `tools` + block 1, which together should clear the minimum, but confirm this\n  in the first logged requests. If `cache_creation_input_tokens` stays at 0 for the\n  static part, the prefix is too small and the cache marker is not doing anything.\n- **Keyword tool groups still change the prefix.** `select_tools()` adds the `plan` or\n  `race` tools when a message mentions their keywords. That changes the `tools` list,\n  which is part of the cached prefix, so such messages still miss the cache. This is\n  not caused by `save_fact` and was not changed here. NOTES.md says the filtering is\n  worth keeping, so the fix would be to keep the tools constant or to move the group\n  tools into a separate cache-controlled position. That is a design decision for you.\n- `MODEL` is `claude-sonnet-4-5`. Not changed.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":849,"cache_read_input_tokens":32859,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":849},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"960d2a77-ac07-4a68-948e-956610a517ec","uuid":"2ad56dc2-0027-4dd2-99d6-a23bae1af4a7","tim