{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtRSieZHgzhZNHrtm1MJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A `save_fact` no longer evicts the static instructions from the prompt cache. I haven't measured the effect against the API, so the fix is unverified in production.\n\n**Cause:** `build_system()` in `bot.py` put the static coaching rules and the per-athlete context, including the `facts` list, into a single cached block. Every `save_fact` changed that block, so the whole prompt was rewritten.\n\n**Change:** `build_system()` now returns two blocks:\n- The static `INSTRUCTIONS`, with the cache marker. This is identical for every athlete and every day.\n- The per-athlete context (date, zones, goal, facts, language), without a marker. This is the only part a memory write changes.\n\nA stub-LLM test confirmed the static block is byte-identical before and after a `save_fact`. I stubbed `save_athlete` so `data/athletes.json` wasn't written, and I reverted the usage-log and `__pycache__` side effects from the test.\n\n**Open points, also in ANSWER.md:**\n- **Minimum cache size:** the static block is about 2,500 characters, which may be under the model's minimum cacheable length on its own. The breakpoint still covers the tools list plus that block, which should clear the minimum. Check that `cache_creation_input_tokens` is non-zero for the static part in the first logged requests.\n- **Keyword tool groups:** `select_tools()` changes the tools list for `plan` and `race` messages. That list is part of the cached prefix, so those messages still miss the cache. I left this alone because NOTES.md says the filtering is worth keeping; fixing it is a design choice for you.\n\nI haven't committed anything. The change is in `bot.py` and the write-up is in `ANSWER.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2170,"cache_read_input_tokens":33708,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2170},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"960d2a77-ac07-4a68-948e-956610a517ec","uuid":"b90889be-aebe-489b-ba4e-133678c099a9","timestamp":"2026-11-10T02:00:47.404Z","request_id":"req_011CgtRSiU8tRfs1hVUh7A9J"}
